    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0488" n="230" xml:id="pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/4737</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.50 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Bride and Hays, representing importers of German goods, have succeeded in
                    obtaining permits for their clients covering German goods ordered prior March 1
                    under circumstances rendering purchaser liable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
